A||||6||RiceCooker||"Buried" (it's another poem)||||2||
Z||000000||RiceCooker||01-02-2001||11:13 PM||||For those of you who have enjoyed my poems, I thought I would post another recent one. This one is very structural - the shape of the poem and the words have much to do with it's meaning. Please let me know what you think. Thanks, Todd<P>The dots are supposed to be spaces (the program won't let me use spaces)<BR>-------<BR>Buried<BR>-------<P>Love<BR>Beauty<BR>Tranquility  <BR>Suddenly come<BR>Crashing down <BR>No time to react <BR>The wave Hits <BR>Overwhelmed with<BR>An agony so deep, it <BR>Bleeds from my every pore<BR>Buried in what was once forever, <BR>Now never, if you were near you would <BR>Have answered my cries, but long escaped................................YOU left<BR>ME.......alone in here to die, an e t e r n i t y  <BR>Has gone by, so why do I still love you, why?<P>It seems I have discovered a hidden talent that I never knew I had. <BR>Don't worry I'm still a full blown fieroholic.<P>[This message has been edited by RiceCooker (edited 01-02-2001).]<P>[This message has been edited by RiceCooker (edited 01-02-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by RiceCooker (edited 01-02-2001).]||||reg||2
Z||000001||Philphine||01-03-2001||02:29 AM||||wacka lacka boom <BR>wrap my hair around a spoon<BR>i may not be the best<BR>but i won't be like the rest<P><BR>some people think my talent should stay buried <P>actually i used to try writing poetry, but some combo of my mother dying and a girlfriend i gave heartfelt poetry to that she said she didn't get ("whadda ya mean?") kinda made me stop. ||||reg||1
