Z||000004||RiceCooker||01-04-2001||01:25 PM||||Awwww, shucks Cheever you're making me blush.<P>I thought I would explain the poem a bit in case it seems a bit abstract.<P>The shape of the poem can be symbolized as a rockslide or an avalanche which is a metaphor for the relationship that came down so suddenly. The "YOU left" part is way over to the right meaning that that person escaped before it hit while the "ME....alone" is trapped under all the rubble of the relationship that is no more.<BR>If you read it a couple times it all makes sense. <P>Did anyone interpret it this way, the 1st time?<P>Thanks, <BR>Todd||||reg||1
